ure  but what i do think is that the market  is drastically overestimating how  confident and persistent the fed's going  to be in these interest rate hikes and  in quantitative tightening i think that  at some point before the market realizes  it the federal reserve's going to give  up they're going to wave that white flag  they simply cannot continue to increase  the price of capital and they cannot  continue to conduct quantitative  tightening forever they also can't do it  for the next two to three years as they  continue to say the federal reserve can  only continue to increase interest rates  so much if they continue on this path  and they don't let up there's a lot of  people that are going to walk into that  voting booth in november and they're  gonna vote out every single person that  appointed these officials ultimately  what we are watching right now is that  the federal reserve they're in control  every asset correlation is going towards  one it all has become one big trade but  at the end of the day the federal  reserve they're gonna have to cut rates  they're gonna have to return to loose  monetary policy the big question in  financial markets right now is when are  they gonna do it 75 basis points that's  a big boy rate hike today but i don't  think this is going to become the norm i  actually think they're going to give up  way before most other people think so
 

